":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":91.3,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.300998464077072,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.14329212262029634,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":96.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03363571912739971,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":8.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0003701515808494148,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":99.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.09288,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":61.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.077,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":7.7,"pf":["flagged"],"description_full":"StoneX Group Inc. operates as a global financial services network that connects companies, organizations, traders, and investors to a market ecosystem in the United States, Europe, South America, the Middle East, Asia, and internationally. The company operates through four segments: Commercial, Institutional, Self-Directed/Retail, and Payments. The Commercial segment provides risk management and hedging, voice brokerage, market intelligence, physical trading, and commodity financing, marketing, procurement, logistics, and price management services; and engages in the risk management and hedging services, execution and clearing of exchange-traded and OTC products. This segment also acts as an institutional dealer in fixed income securities to serve asset managers, commercial bank trust and investment departments, broker-dealers, and insurance companies; and engages in asset management business. The Self-Directed/Retail segment provides trading services and solutions in the global financial markets, including spot foreign exchange, precious metals trading, contracts for differences, and spread bets; and wealth management services, as well as offering physical gold and other precious metals in various forms and denominations through Stonexbullion.com. The company was formerly known as INTL FCStone Inc. and changed its name to StoneX Group Inc. in July 2020. StoneX Group Inc. was founded in 1924 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Philip Andrew Smith | Group CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $25.0M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $816K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["StoneX Group Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.4B market cap on $132.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 142% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 133-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 3% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $4.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 14.35\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (92% sell ratio, net $31.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Financial Services peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 91% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"StoneX Group Inc. $SNEX Stock Purchased by Voya Investment Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/stonex-group-inc-snex-stock-purchased-by-voya-investment-management-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795175933.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"StoneX Group Inc. $SNEX Shares Purchased by Public Sector Pension Investment Board","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/stonex-group-inc-snex-shares-purchased-by-public-sector-pension-investment-board.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795175932.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"StoneX Group Inc. $SNEX Stock: Teachers Retirement System of The State of Kentucky Grows Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/stonex-group-inc-snex-stock-teachers-retirement-system-of-the-state-of-kentucky-grows-position.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795171383.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"StoneX Group Inc. Investigation Notice: SueWallSt Notifies Investors of Pending Investigation Into StoneX Group Inc. (SNEX)","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/stonex-group-inc-investigation-notice-suewallst-notifies-investors-of-pending-investigation-into-stonex-group-inc-snex-302946203.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795138920.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.474,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[